      "data": {
        "text": "All the requested Python files have been created successfully in the current working directory. Here are the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] publish_event.py** - Publishes a JSON event to an AWS SNS topic.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] consume_event.py** - Consumes one message from an AWS SQS queue.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] dead_letter.py** - Sends failed messages to an AWS SQS dead-letter queue.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] batch_publish.py** - Publishes a batch of messages to an AWS SNS topic.\n5. **[HELPER] messaging_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for AWS SNS and SQS.\n6. **[HELPER] messaging_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for AWS SNS and SQS.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] message_summary.py** - Summarizes message processing results.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] message_safety.py** - Checks message payload text for unsafe content.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] payload_translate.py** - Translates customer-facing message payload text.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] message_audit_store.py** - Persists processed message records for later lookup.\n\nEach scored file uses AWS as the concrete external provider, as required.",
